						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														Okay this is a pretty rough idea, but I've talked it over with a few of you in game and some of the other officership.  <br />
<br />
It stems from our need to bolster recruitment.  The best way would be to just open the recruiting up to anyone and everyone, the only problem at that point is we end up getting some pretty terrible players.  <br />
<br />
So...<br />
<br />
I've created a storage character in Freeport.  His name is Cabel, his primary goal is to equip all of our newest members.  Now we have a block of cheese to offer new membership :).  Just to start getting him loaded up I'm going to start taking some basic donations.  THESE ARE NOT REQUIRED OF ANYONE, hence the name donations.  If you WANT to donate, please do.  <br />
<br />
Current donations should be composed of the following list:<br />
<br />
1.)  Newbie Jewelry.  +2, or +3 stuff for ears and rings.  Mostly Int, Wis, Str.<br />
<br />
2.)  Lockjaw hide vests.  These are great newbie fare, the 12ac just can't be beat until your midtwenties.<br />
<br />
3.)  Pelts, pelts, pelts.  I have a very good tailor and will be making full sets of reinforced armor, and banded armor.  Medium or High Quality only please.<br />
<br />
4.)  Silks, silks, silks.  Spiderling silks, silk cords, Spider silks, silk patches.  Anything.  The raw silk newbie caster armor is some of the best for the buck at lower levels.  Plus monks with a full set of cured silk just tend to rock.<br />
<br />
5.)  Cash, whatever you feel is necessary.  Most of this will be spent on a basic &quot;cash allowance&quot; for food and maybe enough to buy a nice piece of armor in Ecomms.<br />
<br />
6.)  Fine Steel weapons.  I know we all see em drop all the time, but have you ever equipped a 5th-10th level character with one.  Pretty nice effect.  Taking you basics though 2-handed, longswords, mace, staffs.  <br />
<br />
7.)  Split Paw armor, found quite a bit when i was hunting in South Karana.  Drops pretty frequently.  Looks and feels nice on my druid.<br />
Plus the Split paw skins get you a nice set of gloves.<br />
<br />
Now pretty much I will be writing down what everyone has donated.  Then at that point you'll obtain the option to &quot;voucher&quot; someone into the guild.  We'll pretty much give them a simple quest to finish off.  Like take this Short beer to (insert name of distant town).  And bring back the item he gives you.  This way we know that they have some decent travel knowledge.<br />
<br />
I think that this incentive package will help us draw the right kind of people into the guild.  Plus give our newbies that are in the guild already.<br />
<br />
thanks for reading<br />
<br />
<br />
Thadius<br />
<br />
RaidNight leader---Newbie recruitment<br />
<br />
<br />
PS Sunday lets take a trip over to Vellious and get us guildies some totems.  I'll be on sometime Sunday afternoon.  See you there.						</td>
